==Latin==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{m|la|de}} + {{m|la|inde}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈde.in.de/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-deinde.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Adverb===
{{la-adv|deinde||-}}

# from that place
# [[thereafter]], [[thereupon]], [[afterwards]], [[then]], from there onwards
#: '''''Deinde''' Cornelia sedet in horto.''
#:: '''Then''' Cornelia sits in the garden.
# and then, [[next]]

